      "qid": "vm_02",
      "question": "First apply zoom_x_region(start=2014, end=2016). Then apply detect_anomalies(threshold=2). Inside that window, do any country-year points count as outliers relative to the whole-series mean, and what does the zoomed shape say about the 2015 dip people often talk about?",
      "question_style": "tool_hinted",
      "ground_truth": {
        "task_type": "vague_multi",
        "answer": {
          "type": "open_ended",
          "value": "Against the entire timeline, nothing crosses the two-sigma rule—so the anomaly layer stays empty even after zooming. Within 2014–2016 you can still read the mid-decade sag and rebound in electricity access as a regional story inside the band, not as a machine-flagged spike."
        },
        "key_insights": [
          "The global mean/std anomaly test does not flag any points in this dataset.",
          "The 2014–2016 window is still useful for eyeballing the dip-and-recovery pattern without relying on red markers."
        ],
        "reasoning_trace": [
          {
            "iteration": 1,
            "capability": "view.domain.zoom",
            "rationale": "Narrows the time axis to the shock-and-recovery years."
          },
          {
            "iteration": 2,
            "capability": "analysis.anomalies.detect",
            "rationale": "Checks for extreme residuals versus the overall series distribution."
          }
        ],
